==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/truː/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-tro.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|tro|trō}}, from {{inh|sv|non|trú}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*trūwō}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|c|-}}

# [[belief]] (that something is true or real (without being perfectly certain))
#: {{ux|sv|Min '''tro''' är att han är skyldig|My '''belief''' is that he's guilty}}
#: {{ux|sv|hennes '''tro''' på tomten|her '''belief''' in Santa Claus}}
# [[belief]], [[faith]], [[trust]] (thinking that someone is reliable or telling the truth)
#: {{ux|sv|blind '''tro''' på auktoriteter|blind '''faith''' in authorities}}
# [[belief]], [[faith]] (thinking that someone or something will or has the capacity to do well or turn out well)
#: {{ux|sv|Jag vill känna '''tro''' på framtiden|I want to have '''faith''' in the future}}
#* {{quote-song|sv|author=w:Marie Fredriksson|year=1996|album=w:I en tid som vår|trans-album=In a time like ours|title=[[w:Tro (song)|Tro]]|trans-title=Faith|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s3hWIJ8ylXs|text='''Tro'''. Jag vill känna '''tro'''. Jag vill känna morgondagen nalkas här i lugn och ro.|t='''Faith''' [ambiguous, but likely faith in the future going on the rest of the lyrics]. I want to feel '''faith'''. I want to feel tomorrow approaching [in, not to] here with peace of mind (in peace and tranquility).}}
# [[religious]] [[faith]]
#: {{ux|sv|den kristna '''tron'''|the Christian '''faith'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|vara stark i '''tron'''|be strong in the '''faith'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|Ingen kultur eller civilisation utan '''tro''' på gudar|No culture or civilization without '''faith''' in gods}}
# {{lb|sv|dated}} [[allegiance]]
#: {{ux|sv|svära konungen '''tro''' och loven|swear allegiance to the king}}

=====Usage notes=====
The base meaning is ''belief'' (compare the verb below). Swedish does not use a separate word for religious faith. Context dictates whether religious faith, belief in something else, or for example faith in the future (belief that the future will turn out okay) is meant.

